# DWT data handling

- There is no backend. Data is either static mock data in `app/data/` (e.g. `regulators-data.js`, `pat-submissions.js`) or held in `req.session.data`.
- Records added during a session (e.g. software providers) are stored as a list under a key that is unique to the version, such as `softwareProvidersV4`. This stops data from one version appearing in another. Create the list on first use inside the version's route function, as `providerList(req)` does.
- Form values are read from `req.body` in the route and validated there. They are only written to session data once valid.
- Helpers for creating, finding and changing records live in `app/data/` (e.g. `software-providers.js`). Reuse them rather than rewriting the logic in the route.
- Fixed example data for demo pages (e.g. `sp.exampleProviders`) is kept separate from session data.
- There are no "check your answers" pages in this prototype. Pages show saved records directly (e.g. the provider detail page).
- "Clear data" in the footer resets session data between research sessions.
- Treat all session data as non-production, test data (see the general core rules). API keys, client IDs, company names and email addresses must be synthetic — never real ones.
